    <div class="osi-modal-head">
      <h3 id="osi-modal-title">The seven layers, with and without Pilot.</h3>
      <p class="osi-modal-sub">Same model. Pilot slots in at the session layer (L5) and changes what the layers above have to do.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="osi-table" role="table" aria-label="OSI layer comparison">
      <div class="osi-row osi-head-row" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="columnheader">Layer</div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-without" role="columnheader">Without Pilot</div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-with" role="columnheader">With Pilot</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L7</span> <span class="osi-lname">Application</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-without" role="cell" data-label="Without Pilot">HTTP APIs, REST, GraphQL. A browser renders pages for a human to click.</div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-with" role="cell" data-label="With Pilot">Agents address peers without requiring a browser or workflow-specific API gateway. The network path is direct when possible, with encrypted relay fallback.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row" role="row">
