        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-with" role="cell" data-label="With Pilot">Compact binary wire format. No JSON parse on the hot path.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row osi-row-hilite" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L5</span> <span class="osi-lname">Session</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-without" role="cell" data-label="Without Pilot">TLS handshakes through public CAs. HTTP sessions. Cookies.</div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-with" role="cell" data-label="With Pilot"><b>Pilot Protocol</b> overlay. 48-bit virtual addresses (<code>N:NNNN.HHHH.LLLL</code>) resolved by a registry - no DNS. Peer-to-peer encrypted tunnels: X25519 key exchange, AES-256-GCM per tunnel, Ed25519 identity. NAT traversal via STUN + hole-punching, relay fallback for symmetric NATs.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row osi-row-green" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L4</span> <span class="osi-lname">Transport</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-without" role="cell" data-label="Without Pilot">TCP. Three-way handshake. Head-of-line blocking.</div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-with" role="cell" data-label="With Pilot">UDP with Pilot's own reliable streams on top: sliding window, AIMD congestion control, SACK.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row osi-row-same" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L3</span> <span class="osi-lname">Network</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-span" role="cell">Same - IPv4 / IPv6. Pilot packets ride real IP between nodes; the overlay sits above, it doesn't replace it.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row osi-row-same" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L2</span> <span class="osi-lname">Data Link</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-span" role="cell">Same - Ethernet, Wi-Fi, whatever the OS hands you.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="osi-row osi-row-same" role="row">
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-layer" role="cell"><span class="osi-ly">L1</span> <span class="osi-lname">Physical</span></div>
        <div class="osi-cell osi-cell-span" role="cell">Same - cables, fiber, radio.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="osi-modal-foot">
      Pilot doesn't replace the stack - it inserts at L5 and lets the layers above serve machines instead of humans.
    </div>
  </div>
